# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. The decision step writes an unstamped terminal for
# the first source shard ahead of the stamped per-shard broadcast - the shape
# of every terminal written outside AtomicWriteGrain's broadcast, which carries
# a count of 0. The receiver takes it down the legacy path and marks the saga
# on it alone, before the other shard's prepare has arrived.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingDecisionShipsUncountedTerminal
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the origin's decision step ships an unstamped terminal ahead of the stamped broadcast, so the receiver marks early
PERTURBS: OriginDecide

--- FIND
OriginDecide ==
    /\ Origin!DecideTx(T)
    /\ UNCHANGED xvars
--- REPLACE
OriginDecide ==
    /\ Origin!DecideTx(T)
\* MUTATION: an unstamped terminal is written with the decision.
    /\ outbox' = outbox \cup {Term(k1, Origin!AllAcked(T), 0)}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<xtree, oext, orcv, dlv, rconn, leafVars, registryVars, barrierVars, lossVars>>
--- END
